response data in a JSON object rather than returning a bare array, which improves flexibility for future changes without breaking client-side code. A mapping of HTTP methods (GET, POST, DELETE) to their expected status codes and response shapes is also provided.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_br7HigaLH0/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-06T14:14:21.000Z"},{"id":"Ehmy68SM8","title":"REST API Requests Explained Clearly | System Design | 7","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gLv5czPnc18","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/rest-api-requests-explained-clearly-system-design-7-ehmy68sm8","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gLv5czPnc18/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T11:53:23.000Z"},{"id":"JfZ8HZCRJ","title":"End of Vibe Coding?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TKal4pZHr0U","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/end-of-vibe-coding--jfz8hzcrj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TKal4pZHr0U/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T07:09:15.000Z"},{"id":"0KO80L4S7","title":"AWS Cloud Deployment: Deploy Spring Boot via ECS, ECR & Elastic Beanstalk","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ydL5NSrWfAk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/aws-cloud-deployment-deploy-spring-boot-via-ecs-ecr-elastic-beanstalk-0ko80l4s7","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ydL5NSrWfAk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29T13:10:43.000Z"},{"id":"DWqVJSZLN","title":"What is an API? Types of APIs Explained | System Design | 6","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UmYVFGCwg2w","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-an-api-types-of-apis-explained-system-design-6-dwqvjszln","summary":"An introductory overview of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) covering what they are and why they exist, followed by explanations of five major API types: REST (using JSON), SOAP (using XML, common in legacy systems), GraphQL (single endpoint with query language), gRPC (protocol buffers, efficient for microservices), and WebSockets (bidirectional real-time communication). Real-world examples like Google Maps integration in Uber/Zomato and chat/notification systems are used to illustrate concepts.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UmYVFGCwg2w/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T14:27:40.000Z"},{"id":"RUTH7SrGX","title":"How to run Gemma 4 locally as a free GitHub Copilot replacement","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CyiqH3SoqBM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/stop-paying-for-ai-using-gemma-4-ruth7srgx","summary":"A walkthrough on replacing paid AI coding subscriptions (GitHub Copilot, Gemini) by running Google's Gemma 4 locally using LM Studio or Ollama. Covers downloading and setting up Gemma 4, configuring LM Studio as a local server, connecting it to VS Code via the Roo Code extension, and using it as a free coding assistant with agent capabilities. Also discusses trade-offs: local models have a knowledge cutoff, require decent hardware (GPU with 12GB+ VRAM recommended), and need manual setup for internet access or fine-tuning.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/CyiqH3SoqBM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-16T08:59:11.000Z"},{"id":"ul7LDNJK3","title":"Vectors Embeddings | Spring AI","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=InMdwHLfopA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/vectors-embeddings-spring-ai-ul7ldnjk3","summary":"A tutorial covering vector embeddings in the context of AI engineering using Spring AI and Mistral's embedding models. Explains how text is tokenized, converted to token IDs, and then transformed into multi-dimensional float vectors that capture semantic relationships between words. Demonstrates the concept visually with 2D plots showing similar words clustering together, then walks through a practical implementation using Spring AI with Mistral's embedding API, including setting up API keys, adding Maven dependencies, and calling the embedding model to get float array representations of text.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/InMdwHLfopA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-13T14:20:35.000Z"},{"id":"rgl0r87mG","title":"Telusko LMS","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ymF28CvKcLM","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/telusko-lms-rgl0r87mg","summary":"Telusko has launched its own Learning Management System (LMS) at telusko.com, moving away from a third-party platform. Users need to create new accounts on the new system. The platform will feature AI-related capabilities and new courses, starting with a 12-week complete DevOps boot camp delivered as weekly recorded content.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ymF28CvKcLM/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-09T11:52:57.000Z"},{"id":"h5iWjQAAQ","title":"12-week DevOps bootcamp covering cloud and infrastructure tools","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JiuujYQdNHY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/complete-devops-bootcamp-master-devops-in-12-weeks-h5iwjqaaq","summary":"A promotional announcement for a 12-week DevOps bootcamp covering tools like Linux, Bash scripting, AWS, Terraform, Ansible, Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins, Git, and Maven. Targets beginners and career switchers looking to enter the DevOps field through a structured, hands-on program.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/JiuujYQdNHY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-08T16:37:41.000Z"},{"id":"SXWzVUX7v","title":"OpenAI shuts down Sora app and Disney deal collapses","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lT2BbB9riik","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/openai-just-shutdown-sora-sxwzvux7v","summary":"OpenAI is shutting down the Sora app, which also collapses a deal with Disney. The author reflects on concerns around AI video generation including high compute costs, copyright issues, and deepfakes. While Sora's shutdown is notable, alternatives like Google Veo exist. The author believes third-party tools built on OpenAI's video API may struggle, and that humans remain cheaper than AI for video creation for now.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lT2BbB9riik/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-03-26T10:23:20.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["stephenwolfram","threatinteractive","vuemastery","jherr","dotnet"],"opposite_handles":["alexfinn","tbpn","kloss_xyz","ryolu_","patrickc"],"similar":[{"id":"stephenwolfram","handle":"stephenwolfram","name":"Stephen Wolfram Writings","is_squad":false,"x":-7.8718,"y":-9.2078,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":40,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/cb389904d1a6411c82feea4a329b90d5","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.265856,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0125,"avg_read_time":41.225,"tag_diversity":0.8},"top_tags_preview":[["ai",12],["physics",10],["machine-learning",8]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.3676,0.3382],"cadence_depth":[-5.5147,9.6471],"hype_variety":[2.4706,-2.0441],"title_style":[5.7794,-1.8824]}},{"id":"threatinteractive","handle":"threatinteractive","name":"Threat Interactive","is_squad":false,"x":-7.7536,"y":-9.2627,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":30,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--WbpDdGC8--/f_auto/v1734606725/logos/threatinteractive","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.447924,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":15.466667,"tag_diversity":0.333333},"top_tags_preview":[["unreal-engine",19],["game-development",19],["graphics-programming",11]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.6471,3.9265],"cadence_depth":[-6.7059,8.1029],"hype_variety":[-4.4706,-9.2941],"title_style":[-4.5735,-1.2794]}},{"id":"vuemastery","handle":"vuemastery","name":"Vue Mastery","is_squad":false,"x":-7.5801,"